# Task: Add an automatic itch.io build to the `moo` game, modelled on Alva's

You are working in two repositories by hiyroscript:

- **`hiyroscript/moo`** — the game to change. It was called **Mimblumi** and has since been renamed **Mavooli** (package name `mavooli`, logo `mavooli.png`). Whenever this task says "the game", it means this one. Use the current name, **Mavooli**, in everything you create (file names, ZIP name, workflow name, docs), and do not bring back "Mimblumi" anywhere.
- **`hiyroscript/alva`** — the reference. It already has an automatic itch.io build. **Read it, do not change it.**

The goal: every push to `main` in `moo` (and a manual "Run workflow") builds an itch.io-ready HTML5 ZIP of Mavooli, validates it, and keeps it as a downloadable artifact on the GitHub Actions run, exactly like Alva does, so the owner can upload it to itch.io where players will play it in the browser. The existing GitHub Pages deployment must keep working unchanged.

