## Step 1 — An itch.io build of the game (relative paths)

GitHub Pages serves Mavooli from `/moo/` (`base: '/moo/'` in `vite.config.ts`), and `index.html` uses root-absolute paths (`/favicon.ico`, `/hs.jpg`, `/mavooli.png`, `/src/main.ts`…). itch.io serves the game inside an `<iframe>` from an unpredictable sub-path on `html-classic.itch.zone`, so the itch.io build must use **relative** URLs everywhere.

- Make `vite.config.ts` choose `base` by mode: keep `'/moo/'` for the default/Pages build, and use `'./'` for a new `itch` mode (e.g. `vite build --mode itch`), writing to `dist/itch/` instead of `dist/`. Keep every other existing option (`cssMinify: false`, `chunkSizeWarningLimit: 700`, comments). The Pages build output must stay byte-for-byte what it is today.
- Make sure every asset the game uses ends up relative in the itch build: images imported through TypeScript (`mavooli.png`, `hs.jpg` via `images.d.ts`), the favicon, the apple-touch-icon, the preloads. Files referenced only from `index.html` with absolute `/…` paths must either be moved to `public/`, imported, or otherwise resolved so they are emitted with relative URLs. Verify in the built `dist/itch/index.html` that **no** `src`/`href` starts with `/` or with `http`.
- Check the code for anything that assumes the `/moo/` path or the top-level window (e.g. `location.pathname`, hot-reload position saving, `history`, fullscreen, pointer lock, focus). It must run inside a cross-origin iframe. Wrap `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` access in try/catch if it is not already, since itch.io's iframe may block third-party storage.
- Keyboard focus: on itch.io keys only reach the game after it is focused. Make sure a click/tap on the canvas (and the intro's "Press to start") focuses the game so WASD/arrow keys work immediately, and that arrow keys and Space do not scroll the itch.io page (`preventDefault` where the game uses them).
- Respect all of moo's README rules: one font `var(--font)`, three.js pinned to r128, set-up order in `main.ts`, the order of random draws is the world (do not add, remove or reorder any `rng()` call), start-up work goes through `Loader`.

## Step 2 — Tools: `tools/itch/` in moo

Create Node ESM scripts (no new runtime dependencies; dev tools only, Node 22+, built-in modules where possible), following Alva's structure and style:

- **`tools/itch/build.mjs`** — empties `dist/itch/`, runs the type check and the Vite itch build, validates the folder, and only if valid writes **`dist/mavooli-itch.zip`** (with `index.html` at the ZIP root, no enclosing folder), validates the archive against the folder, and prints a report (files, sizes, totals against itch.io's limits, archive size). Any problem → exit code 1 and no archive left behind. Ends by printing `OK`.
- **`tools/itch/zip.mjs`** — a deterministic ZIP writer adapted from Alva's (fixed entry order, fixed timestamps, CRC-32), so the same commit always makes the same ZIP. Reuse Alva's code where it fits.
- **`tools/itch/validate.mjs`** — runnable on its own (validates an existing `dist/`), checking, as Alva does:
  - itch.io limits: fewer than 1,000 files (warn above 950), ≤ 500 MB total, ≤ 200 MB per file, paths ≤ 240 characters, no two names differing only in case, plain characters only.
  - `index.html` at the root; every local URL referenced by `index.html`, the CSS and the JS bundle exists in the folder under its exact name (case-sensitive), and none is root-absolute.
  - Nothing development-only: no `src/`, `tools/`, `.github/`, `node_modules/`, source maps, `.ts` files, Markdown, `package.json`, `max`, or `.git`.
  - No other host (adapt `hosts.mjs`): no script, style, image, font or fetch from any `http(s)://`/`ws(s)://` address; only player-opened links, if any, are allowed and must be listed explicitly.
  - The archive: every entry intact (CRC-32), exactly the folder's files and bytes, `index.html` at its root, no unsafe paths (`..`, absolute, backslashes).
- **`tools/itch/verify.mjs`** (the equivalent of Alva's `verify:itch`) — serves `dist/itch/` from a tiny built-in Node static server **under a nested, unrelated sub-path** (to imitate itch.io) and checks that every file the page references is served with HTTP 200 and the right content type. If a headless browser is available in CI without new heavy dependencies, also load the page inside a cross-origin `<iframe>` and assert no console errors; otherwise keep it to the HTTP-level check and say so in the docs. Alva's simulation-equivalence approach does not apply to Mavooli and must not be ported.

Add to `package.json` scripts: `"build:itch": "node tools/itch/build.mjs"` and `"verify:itch": "node tools/itch/verify.mjs"`. Keep `dev`, `build`, `preview`, `typecheck` unchanged. If you add a test runner, use `node --test` like Alva with tests under `tests/` (e.g. a test that the itch `index.html` has only relative URLs and that `zip.mjs` round-trips), and run them in CI.

## Step 3 — The workflow: `.github/workflows/itch-release.yml` in moo

Mirror Alva's file, with a header comment in the same style explaining what it does and that it never uploads anything by itself:

```yaml
name: itch.io release
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
permissions:
  contents: read
jobs:
  release:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 30
    steps:
      - checkout (same action major version deploy.yml uses)
      - setup-node, node-version 22, cache: npm
      - npm ci
      - node --test   (only if you added tests)
      - npm run build:itch
      - npm run verify:itch
      - actions/upload-artifact@v4:
          name: mavooli-itch-${{ github.sha }}
          path: dist/mavooli-itch.zip
          if-no-files-found: error
          compression-level: 0
```

Then add an **optional automatic push to itch.io with butler**, modelled on the `itch` job in Alva's `release.yml`: a second job (`needs: release`) that downloads the artifact, and only if the secret `BUTLER_API_KEY` **and** the repository variable `ITCH_PROJECT` (e.g. `hiyroscript/mavooli`) are set, downloads butler from `https://broth.itch.zone/butler/linux-amd64/LATEST/archive/default`, prints `butler -V`, and runs `butler push dist/mavooli-itch.zip "$ITCH_PROJECT:html" --userversion "<package.json version>-<short sha>"`. When either is missing, emit a `::notice::` saying no upload happened and succeed. Never print the key. Use `concurrency` so two pushes to the channel never overlap.

Do not touch `deploy.yml` beyond what is strictly needed; both workflows run independently on every push to `main`. `dist/` is already in `.gitignore`; keep it that way.

